# Firebase — this app initializes Firebase entirely from Dart
# (lib/firebase_options.dart, committed with real values), never from these
# native config files. `flutterfire configure` generates them by default
# alongside the Google Services Gradle plugin; on Android, applying that
# plugin makes Firebase auto-initialize a "[DEFAULT]" app via
# FirebaseInitProvider before our own Firebase.initializeApp() call runs,
# which then throws "FirebaseApp name [DEFAULT] already exists!" — so the
# plugin/these files are deliberately left out. See docs/ios-dev-setup.md.
**/android/app/google-services.json
**/ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist
**/firebase.json

# Go (chat server)
/server/roost-server
vendor/

# Kubernetes / Helm local overrides
*.local.yaml
